    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by an elite 87.14 efficiency rating for **Corbin Carroll**, who faces Mikolas in a quintessential \"green light\" matchup. With Mikolas\u2019s slow delivery providing a distinct advantage for base-stealing, **Corbin Carroll** is our primary source of upside in the scarcest category. Alongside him, **James Wood** (69.70) remains a high-floor start despite a neutral platoon split against Drake, primarily because his elite .423 xwOBA minimizes the risk of a total dud. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Isaac Paredes** are both strong plays today (70.58 and 72.13, respectively), as both benefit from favorable, soft-tossing matchups against Mikolas and Fedde, respectively; **Isaac Paredes** in particular sees a significant +9% boost from the platoon advantage against the right-handed Fedde.\n\nOur most difficult decision centered on the utility slot, where **Josh Naylor** (49.91) barely edged out **Seiya Suzuki** (47.00). While **Seiya Suzuki** is a viable talent, the optimizer favored **Josh Naylor**\u2019s core base projection and his protected spot in the #5 hole, even though he faces a formidable opponent in deGrom. The benching of **Cole Young** (39.16) and **Travis Bazzana** (36.57) was a necessary discipline; falling below our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" effectively disqualifies them from active consideration to preserve our precious game caps. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Jose Caballero**, whose 48.26 score is heavily suppressed by a difficult matchup against the left-handed Cristopher S\u00e1nchez and his elite ability to control the running game, which nullifies **Jose Caballero**'s primary value. We will continue to monitor the lineup status for **Jose Caballero** and **Henry Bolte**, the latter of whom is relegated to the bottom of the order and remains a high-risk, low-ceiling play today.",
